  "summary": "The study compares a vacuum-filtered Ti3C2Tx control film with three in-situ dopamine-polymerized Ti3C2Tx/PDA films containing 2%, 5%, or 10% DA. The Ti3C2Tx/PDA-10 composition was additionally tested as a mass-loading series (2.8, 7.3, and 13.6 mg/cm2), treated here as distinct fabricated electrodes because loading was deliberately varied. The headline 13.6 mg/cm2 Ti3C2Tx/PDA-10 electrode delivered 3440 mF/cm2 at 2 mV/s in 1 M H2SO4. BET surface area, pore diameter, porosity, tortuosity, and thicknesses for most films were not reported."
